{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1522635-w5-what-makes-an-elder","id":1522635,"title":"W5 What makes an Elder","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-15T10:52:59-07:00","id":1522635,"title":"W5 What makes an Elder","content":"W5 has a fair bit of talk of the discord between Elders and the newer generation joining the battle against th eWyrm. My question is what defines and Elder. Is it a matter of renown or renown and age? How much renown makes and Elder? Is it based on total renown or a certain amount in a singular category? There are no mention of ranks in the rules but Gifts seem to be organized within tiers. Could it be implied that these tiers are tied to rank? <br /> <br /> As a related question, how fast should PCs gain renown in a chronical. Second question: Should the chronical allow the PCs to become elders themselves? I am wondering as the a lot of the fluff seems to imply that part of the game is the young (the PCs) raging against their elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T11:40:37-07:00","id":1522638,"title":"","content":"Why couldn\u2019t it be just straight age, with no link to Renown? Or maybe the more Renowned elders could be the leaders of their generation. Sort of setting up the whole generational conflict thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T11:56:11-07:00","id":1522639,"title":"","content":"Legacy, but Elder used to mean &quot;of high renown.&quot; So an Elder is someone who has a bunch of renown regardless of their age.<br /> <br /> In W5, though, Elder should be someone who holds onto the values of the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> As for if PCs can become Elders, the game has no support for Elder level game. You should keep renown gains/losses very minimal, as more power the PCs have, the less the game can support the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T05:02:48-07:00","id":1522667,"title":"","content":"Most likely both age and renown. Werewolf the apocalypse 5th speaks clearly about generations of garou. At the same time, it says that it's not known about teenage first changes. We can therefore imagine that a new garou should be changed in the span from 25 to 35 years old.<br /> Taking a look to Crimson Thawn, all the youngs of the pack are around 30 years old or more, and the pack leader seems to be around 50 and it's described as a veteran, for example.<br /> <br /> But it's also about the kind of story you want to tell. Renown doesn't mean necessary middle or old age. A garou that decide to get shit done and is lucky enough can collect a decent amount of renown pretty fast, depending on what he accomplished. It doesn't mean he is old btw. The new edition is about also the chance to change things and put the litany in discussion which most likely means that younger garou can be renowed and change things. If you take a look to the npc also, it's not hard to see high renown antagonists but without exceptional pools.<br /> <br /> My players are relatively young but are collecting renown pretty quick. They have right now around 7 dots of renown, soon 8. We are at the forth part of our chronicle, and they faced <br /> - black spiral dancer pack <br /> - found an important fetish <br /> - re enstabilished an old caern <br /> - made other packs cooperate <br /> - destroyed a militant vampire cult <br /> - destroyed an operation front of an oil company and did a mess with the media <br /> - created their own pack after they discovered shit abut the first pack leader <br /> - established their own caern <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 09-16-2023, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T10:48:58-07:00","id":1522674,"title":"","content":"I get what you are saying <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3773_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3773\" data-vbnamecard=\"3773\">Helur</a>. Still wish the game was a little more definitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T15:40:20-07:00","id":1522680,"title":"","content":"In the Wise Words of W5... &quot;Who knows?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T23:32:50-07:00","id":1522687,"title":"","content":"Elders are, going by the book, something to be opposed and as you can see the word Elder is very rarely without a negative qualifier in the text. So prettymuch anyone who sees value in parts of the Litany or Nation is going to be referred to as an Elder.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T08:05:18-07:00","id":1522702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1522635-w5-what-makes-an-elder?p=1522687#post1522687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elders are, going by the book, something to be opposed and as you can see the word Elder is very rarely without a negative qualifier in the text. So prettymuch anyone who sees value in parts of the Litany or Nation is going to be referred to as an Elder.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To add to that: In the case of Harano and Hauglosk (pg 51 - 53), each time two of the three examples talk about the Pack dealing with a more renowned, more experienced Garou whose troublesome behavior reflects them suffering from Harano or Hauglosk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}